Fix tab selection in the Other windows popover and toggle the bookmark overflow menu

- Preserve selected tabs from every browser window during the main list render. In horizontal current-window-only mode, the old cleanup only considered the current window, so Ctrl-click and Shift-click selections from the Other windows popover were immediately cleared. The popover keeps using the same Ctrl/Shift selection logic as the vertical list.
- Make the bookmark bar's “»” overflow popup close when the same button is clicked again.
- Exempt the overflow trigger from menu outside-dismiss handling, so the menu is still present when its second click handler runs. Other folder/context menus do not inherit the overflow-toggle ownership.

Validation: content.js, fn-bookmarks.js, and fn-menu.js pass JavaScript syntax parsing. Source checks confirm background selections are retained and the overflow trigger can receive the second click. No live browser UI test was run.
